==English==
[[Image:Amaryllis_belladonna_sfbg_1.jpg|thumb|right|200px|{{taxlink|Amaryllis belladonna|species}}]]

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|la|-}} {{m|mul|Amaryllis}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˌæməˈɹɪlɪs/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# The {{vern|belladonna lily}}, {{taxlink|Amaryllis belladonna|species}}, native to South Africa.
# A similar lily in genus ''[[Hippeastrum]]'', such as {{taxlink|Hippeastrum puniceum|species}}, and cultivars.

====Usage notes====
The plural {{m|en|amaryllides}} also exists, but is obsolete.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|Amaryllis belladona}} {{vern|belladonna lily}}, {{vern|naked-lady-lily}}, {{vern|Jersey lily}}, {{vern|amarillo|novern=1}}, {{vern|March lily}} {{qualifier|South Africa}}

